01:16:47.161 --> 01:16:47.895
committee while becoming

01:16:47.895 --> 01:16:50.464
immersed in the fillmore music

01:16:50.464 --> 01:16:51.532
scene of the 19 70s.

01:16:51.532 --> 01:16:54.368
>> mark would go on to be a

01:16:54.368 --> 01:16:55.700
pioneer in the asian-american

01:16:55.700 --> 01:16:55.770
jazz movement combining the

01:16:55.770 --> 01:16:57.770
spiritual and improvizational

01:16:58.740 --> 01:16:59.340
elements of jazz with east

01:16:59.340 --> 01:17:01.340
asian instrumentation.

01:17:01.810 --> 01:17:02.677
In addition to the upright

01:17:02.677 --> 01:17:06.130
bass, he became a master of the

01:17:06.130 --> 01:17:06.647
show a mouth organ more

01:17:06.647 --> 01:17:07.381
commonly found in japanese

01:17:07.381 --> 01:17:09.781
traditional music that sounds

01:17:09.951 --> 01:17:10.384
right at home on mark's jazz

01:17:10.384 --> 01:17:12.384
contributions.

01:17:13.488 --> 01:17:14.189
>> he toured internationally

01:17:14.189 --> 01:17:16.189
and frequently collaborated

01:17:17.358 --> 01:17:18.260
